# backend/Dockerfile builds with the REPO ROOT as context (see
# cloudbuild.yaml / the Dockerfile's own top comment: `docker build -f
# backend/Dockerfile .`), so this file has to live here, not inside
# backend/ -- Docker only ever reads a .dockerignore from the build
# context's root.
#
# The Dockerfile only COPYs packedfootball/ and backend/ -- everything
# else here exists purely to keep what Docker tars up and sends to the
# daemon lean, and backend/.env specifically out of the image entirely
# (COPY backend/ backend/ would otherwise ship it straight into the built
# image and the registry it gets pushed to).

.git/
mobile/
backend/.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
